## Summary
The U.S. Supreme Court sided with the Trump administration in a legal dispute concerning mail-in voting. Justice Clarence Thomas also discussed related issues on Senator Ted Cruz's podcast, adding to the ongoing debate.

## Key Points
- The Supreme Court ruled in favor of the Trump administration's position on mail-in voting.
- Justice Thomas's remarks on the podcast highlight judicial perspectives on election procedures.
- Mail-in voting continues to be a politically and legally contentious topic in the U.S.
- High-profile figures like Justice Thomas and Senator Cruz are involved in the discourse.


